    <description>
     <narrative xml:lang="EN">Number of PoEs equipped with mobile labs to facilitate early detection

Number of PoE personnel equipped with relevant knowledge and skills to enhance early detection and management of suspected cases</narrative>
    </description>
    <baseline year="2021">
     <comment>
      <narrative xml:lang="EN">Zero (0)</narrative>
     </comment>
    </baseline>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2021-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2021-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">4 POEs equipped with mobile labs to facilitate early detection</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Needs assessment for the mobile labs conducted in 4 selected sites to provide relevant information on the nature of mobile labs to be procured in all the selected sites</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
    <period>
     <period-start iso-date="2022-01-01"></period-start>
     <period-end iso-date="2022-12-31"></period-end>
     <target>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">Port health staff in designated 4 POEs- Kotoka International Airport, Paga, Elubo and Aflao equipped with relevant training to support early detection and management of public health emergencies-
Mobile laboratories in 4POEs completed</narrative>
      </comment>
     </target>
     <actual>
      <comment>
       <narrative xml:lang="EN">The construction of the mobile laboratory at Aflao has been completed, and construction at the other 3 points of entry- Elubo, Paga and KIA are currently being completed. The trainings for port health staff by Ghana Health Service and Noguchi Memorial Institute for Medical Research (NMIMR) have also been completed and 84 port health staff (61M;33F) have received the requisite training to support early detection and management of public health emergencies in Ghana.</narrative>
      </comment>
     </actual>
    </period>
   </indicator>
